  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This evergreen tree features small, glossy leaves that are aromatic when crushed, making it a great specimen for lessons on plant scents and oils. The dense foliage provides excellent cover for birds and insects, offering opportunities to study local wildlife interactions. Its small, waxy berries can be used to discuss seed dispersal and the role of plants in the food chain. The tree&#x27;s ability to thrive in various soil types and conditions can be a practical example of plant adaptability and resilience.",
